<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pakistan-Taliban conflict: How India could benefit from shifting regional dynamics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f8649bd1cf57bcf0dbdbc3da6a25f742e4e0f5a72c9398330cb7eb369073e5</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426--f7ab516276cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Pakistan's influence in Afghanistan comes under strain, India is rebuilding ties with the Taliban in Kabul. Can New Delhi turn this diplomatic opening into lasting strategic gains?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia frees jailed American Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c7f2c9c2ffacd84fc99297db03ce94cf862da6ea725bbd9942babc29fd25238</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452--b6488d619654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During talks between Vladimir Putin and Steve Witkoff, Putin announced that jailed American Stephen Hubbard had been released. The Kremlin also said Russia was "in principle" ready to resume trilateral talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP Helen Haines loses both legs after car attack as suspect appears in court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e034d8a67f563946a15987597a96b060f8f693a4176e901366d4180219294810</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660--bbf1d96427b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors have amputated both of Helen Haines legs after the Australian lawmaker was hit in an apparent deliberate attack. The suspected driver involved in the attack has appeared in court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK fighter jets to protect Saudi Arabia from Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36cf128f22a5d8ba99074cdc4881bb18666f3f30733491cdf380ac1f40eb5479</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T01:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467--d87226c03f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UK is sending military support to Saudi Arabia as Iran-aligned Houthi rebels launch repeated attacks on the kingdom.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal housing protests continue after police clear camps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2469f5bfb5fd1a45bb432a62a38a3900f622e88a411cb9a589c296eb38464da</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904--9c24875c39a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators vow to continue their campaign to call for affordable housing in Portugal after police cleared tent camps and arrested at least 55 people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0d05cf40bd8550f0e48c300f51785eebb23998071eb5e7b3fe32802744f067a</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon faces uncertainty as UNIFIL mandate nears end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afad535eea7cdf8587737c419b0fc63445dffa736d9ab0b744431a6d095f2714</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491--a12453a4b744.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As UN peacekeeping forces prepare to withdraw from Lebanon, Israel remains present and Hezbollah is still armed. A new EU support mission aims to strengthen Lebanon's army, but will not replace UN peacekeepers.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1a0d6d178bb0971872af574059235646f91b7e013730c3b0688860828167854</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4db01feb6420ae6a3c0a28088268ccf0f3b32a085fd637b1e3e1eb96a448ad3</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU plan for Arctic warily eyes influence of Russia, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:584bdaffd2ae6743ee21358956e44412b0ccd0d4b41e6396ef9f00cf89cf1134</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219--7030ab283919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU unveiled its priorities in the Arctic as it vies with Russia, China and the US for influence. EU foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage undermine Arctic security.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Flavio Bolsonaro tied ahead of runoff vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305538cfe9db421c40dc76da29c6741d7e9697ccdc42192cf139793fe38d7dc5</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182--cfbbc055c58e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With just under a week to go before the decisive presidential runoff election, polls show left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro are virtually tied.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fbc558b536d901dfdc4f151359d2fc3a0cf3eca217bae80ceb67e50de0fff7</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
